<title>USA: General Scanning unit sees victory in patent fight.</title>
<headline>General Scanning unit sees victory in patent fight.</headline>
<dateline>WATERTOWN, MASS. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Scanning Inc said Tuesday it expects to win a patent fight between its View Engineering unit and Robotic Vision Systems Inc.</p>
<p>The company won a patent infringement suit brought by Robotic Vision Systems that involved a method of using three-dimensional sensors to inspect the leads of integrated circuit chips, but a federal appeals court in Washington overturned the ruling and sent it back to a California trial judge.</p>
<p>Robotic Vision said earlier it would vigorously pursue the matter in the lower court.</p>
<p>But Victor Wooley, chief financial officer of General Scanning, said: &quot;We're confident that we'll prevail again.&quot;</p>
</text>
